# Recipe Content

## File layout

```
src/content/recipes/{locale}/{slug}.mdx
```

Locales: `fr` (default), `en`. Each translation pair shares the same `translationKey`.

## Frontmatter schema

Required fields (see `src/content.config.ts`):

- `title`, `description`, `pubDate`, `prepTime`, `cookTime`, `servings`
- `difficulty`: `easy` | `medium` | `hard`
- `translationKey`: shared slug-like key linking fr/en versions
- `ingredients`: array of `{ quantity?, unit?, item }`
- `steps`: array of strings
- `tags`: optional string array

## MDX body

- Write cultural/historical narrative in the MDX body (headings, paragraphs)
- Keep structured data (ingredients, steps, times) in frontmatter — not in prose
- Ingredients without a fixed quantity omit `quantity` (e.g. "salt and pepper")

## Adding a new recipe

1. Create `{locale}/{slug}.mdx` for each locale with matching `translationKey`
2. Schema changes go in `src/content.config.ts` only
3. No page changes needed — `[slug].astro` generates paths from the collection
